# A write and a read through a pointer 260 levels deep (as unit_addr_depth goes through two): the word
# `\\...\p` was taken in at most 255 bytes, and a longer one was refused as "assignment target must be a
# declared typed mutable value" (owner group 3 of the expression text, section 99).  build reads its own n
# afterwards and gets its working 0 (L2 section 18.2).  Success is 7.
